# Team-look cut of the flagship live Claude Code clip (GDK-842 media): one
# vertical take that asks Claude for the team colours plus this release's
# dimension axes — denser rows and a larger body type. No dashboard job —
# charts live in claude-dashboards.tape.
#
# Regenerated by `bash e2e/demo/record-claude-drive.sh vertical claude-tokens`,
# which requires:
#   bash tools/tapes/prepare-claude-drive.sh   (frozen demo home + skill install)
#   vhs, ffmpeg, a Claude Code login
# Run `bash tools/tapes/prepare-claude-drive.sh --clean` afterwards — the
# isolated HOME holds a 0600 copy of this machine's credentials.
#
# Nothing here is scripted output: Claude's commands are the model's. Takes
# vary; the orchestrator re-runs until the result contract holds (at least
# one colour change and one dimension override from ui.tokens reflected in
# the open tab). Everything visible comes from examples/demo.db.
#
# 44px rows: spacing.row's range is 36–56 and row-excerpt must stay ≥ row+8
# (docs/CONFIGURATION.md, dimension axes) — 44 clears both, so the take shows
# a clean pass with nothing to talk back to. Since GDK-858 an out-of-band
# value would be applied with a warning rather than refused, and since
# GDK-853 the ui.tokens.<axis> subpaths merge key-wise, so the whole look can
# land in one pass — the clip no longer has to walk one axis pair at a time.
#
# Vertical-native: unlike claude-drive.tape (which stores the landscape
# original and is rewritten by record-claude-drive.sh), this clip only ever
# ships vertical, so the 1080×520 @ 18px geometry — the same values the
# flagship's rewrite produces, matching FLAGSHIP_V_TERM_H in
# claude-drive-web.spec.ts — lives here directly. The Output path is the
# shared claude-drive-vertical workdir: the web recorder
# (e2e/demo/claude-drive-web.spec.ts) hardcodes it and is clip-agnostic.
# export-claude-drive.sh trims this clip at the raw duration (not at the
# last colour event) because the dimension repaint emits no timeline beat.
#
# Theme: gadak-paper, same identity as mcp.tape / agent.tape / claude-drive.tape.
# Not in `make media` — same reason as claude-drive (live Claude Code login +
# model quota).

Output e2e/.tmp/claude-drive-vertical/term.mp4

Require claude

Set Shell "bash"
Set FontSize 18
Set FontFamily "D2Coding, Menlo, Monaco, monospace"
Set Width 1080
Set Height 520
Set Theme {"name":"gadak-paper","background":"#f4efe4","foreground":"#1c1812","cursor":"#2e4560","selection_background":"#d5dde8","black":"#1c1812","red":"#8f3530","green":"#2f5e42","yellow":"#8a6418","blue":"#2f5d8c","magenta":"#2e4560","cyan":"#2a4159","white":"#e4d9c4","brightBlack":"#635a4f","brightRed":"#8f3530","brightGreen":"#2f5e42","brightYellow":"#8a6418","brightBlue":"#2e4560","brightMagenta":"#2e4560","brightCyan":"#2a4159","brightWhite":"#f4efe4"}
Set Padding 16
Set Framerate 8
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Set WaitTimeout 420s

# Neutral shell: no user@host, no real $HOME path. HOME is the throwaway
# agent home, GADAK_HOME is the frozen capture workspace the serve tab uses.
Hide
Set TypingSpeed 1ms
Type "source tools/tapes/.tmp/env-claude-drive.sh || exit 1"
Enter
Type "python3 /private/tmp/gadak-claude-drive/strip-oauth.py"
Enter
Type "python3 /private/tmp/gadak-claude-drive/mark-epoch.py"
Enter
Type "clear"
Enter
Set TypingSpeed 45ms
Show

Sleep 500ms

Type "claude"
Enter
# TUI boot. 7s — claude-drive.tape take 1 slept 5s and landed on a
# bypass-permissions dialog; keep the longer wait.
Sleep 7s

# User prompt (English, README audience). Same team look as the flagship
# take, plus the dimension asks. Claude's command wording is not scripted.
Type "Give this workspace our team's look: purple accent, green quick-win labels, orange bug chips. Then tighten the layout — denser rows (44px) and a slightly larger body type (14px)."
Sleep 600ms
Enter

# Live model. 300s covers a typical sonnet config pass plus a short hold on
# the retinted, densified tab. Idle tail is cut in export-claude-drive.sh.
# Do not Ctrl+C (that prints a resume UUID — mcp.tape).
Sleep 300s
